From 155695012e2458aa41f74ce482bc809ab19afed2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Alexandr Nedvedicky <sashan@openssl.org>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 15:59:56 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] QUIC client: fix off-path Version Negotiation with wrong SCID
 aborting handshake

An off-path attacker who can forge the server's source address could
make a QUIC client's connection attempt fail by sending one 11-byte
Version Negotiation packet to the client's UDP port.  SSL_connect()
then returned failure with CONNECTION_REFUSED "unsupported protocol
version".  The attacker never saw any traffic.  They need only
the server's address, port, and a correct guess of the client's port,
and the packet had to arrive during the first round trip, before
the client processes the server's first reply.  Nothing crashed,
and servers and connections that have already processed a packet
from the server are not affected.

Add a check for the server SCID matching the initial DCID (and a silent
rejection of the packet silently on mismatch) in the version negotiation
packet handling code path in ch_rx_handle_packet().

Fixes: 78702fb7d63b "Handle the receipt of version negotiation packets"
Original-Commit: e03013166fe5 "QUIC client: fix off-path Version Negotiation with wrong SCID aborting handshake"
Original-PR: https://github.com/openssl/openssl/pull/33490
Reported-by: Anthropic's OSS Scanner (finding ANT-2026-6CXTP19B)
Reviewed-by: Neil Horman <nhorman@openssl.org>
Reviewed-by: Andrew Dinh <andrewd@openssl.org>
Reviewed-by: Eugene Syromiatnikov <esyr@openssl.org>
Merge-date: Mon Nov 23 14:02:01 2026
Merged-from: https://github.com/openssl/openssl/pull/33533
---
 ssl/quic/quic_channel.c | 3 +++
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+)

diff --git a/ssl/quic/quic_channel.c b/ssl/quic/quic_channel.c
index e72ac93..3717f8c 100644
--- a/ssl/quic/quic_channel.c
+++ b/ssl/quic/quic_channel.c
@@ -2496,6 +2496,9 @@ static void ch_rx_handle_packet(QUIC_CHANNEL *ch, int channel_only)
         if (ch->qrx_pkt->hdr->version != 0)
             return;
 
+        if (!ossl_quic_conn_id_eq(&ch->qrx_pkt->hdr->src_conn_id, &ch->init_dcid))
+            return;
+
         /*
          * RFC 9000 s. 6.2: If a client receives a version negotiation
          * packet, we need to do the following:
